    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0392" n="293" xml:id="pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.1121 Simpson, Lawrence/74: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Hamburg</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schnare</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-17T13:00:00-04:00">August 17, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to your despatch No. 499,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d215-f1"/> please
                    express to the appropriate German authorities, unless you have already done so,
                    the hope that Simpson may be given an early trial.</p>
                <p>The Department is likewise interested in knowing what measures have been taken to
                    assure Simpson of adequate legal representation.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph all important developments and supplement with full written
                    reports. You should also keep the Consul General at Berlin and the Embassy fully
                    informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
